    "CVE-2026-97037"
  ],
  "summary": "Building a malicious package that uses cgo could cause arbitrary code execution at link time by passing linker script…",
  "details": "Building a malicious package that uses cgo could cause arbitrary code execution at link time by passing linker script files to the host linker via \"#cgo LDFLAGS\". Split \"-Wl,\" flags that consume a following argument (such as \"-Wl,-rpath\", \"-Wl,--just-symbols\", and \"-Wl,-undefined\") previously accepted a bare second argument without a \"-Wl,\" prefix, which the compiler driver passes directly to the linker as a positional input file. Additionally, when using GNU ld.bfd, flags such as \"-framework\", \"-Wl,-framework\", \"-Wl,-undefined\", \"-Wl,--just-symbols\", \"-Wl,-R\", \"-Wl,-subsystem\", and (on non-Darwin platforms) \"-Wl,-sectcreate\" could cause ld.bfd to interpret their arguments as linker scripts if they named a regular file on disk. The go command now requires a \"-Wl,\" prefix on the second token of split \"-Wl,\" flags (except \"-Wl,-R\"), verifies that these flags do not reference linker script files, and disallows bare \"-Wl,--warn-backrefs-exclude\".",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V3",
      "score": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"
    }
  ],
